          "title": "Occasion and practical layers",
          "source": "Closet Quest project-authored styling guide",
          "origin": "project-authored",
          "excerpt": "For a work meeting, interview, or smart dinner, consider owned structured layers, tidy trousers or a dress, and suitable shoes while respecting the user's stated dress code. For casual outings, prioritize their comfort and preferred style. Add a layer when the user supplies cool-weather context; do not claim to know live weather. If no dress code or temperature is supplied, state the assumption or offer an adaptable option. Avoid promising that an outfit is suitable for every workplace or event.",
