          "documentId": "893ab9ae-a83b-4684-9184-c74b21cf4972",
          "title": "Comfort, silhouette, and color balance",
          "source": "Closet Quest project-authored styling guide",
          "origin": "project-authored",
          "excerpt": "For a comfortable everyday outfit, consider the user's fit preference and preferred footwear. A relaxed top can pair with a more structured bottom, or a fitted top with a relaxed bottom; neither is a requirement. Repeating one color across two owned pieces can make a combination feel coherent. Neutrals can support a stronger color, while a tonal combination uses nearby shades. These are suggestions, not universal rules. Never infer the user's body type, gender, or health from a photo.",
