          "citationId": "KB:893ab9ae-a83b-4684-9184-c74b21cf4971:0",
          "documentId": "893ab9ae-a83b-4684-9184-c74b21cf4971",
          "title": "Build a complete outfit from owned pieces",
          "source": "Closet Quest project-authored styling guide",
          "origin": "project-authored",
          "excerpt": "Start with the user's chosen anchor garment and occasion. A complete outfit usually needs a top and bottom, or a dress, plus shoes. Only recommend garments present in the reviewed wardrobe. A bag, belt, or jacket can support a look but does not replace its core pieces. If the wardrobe cannot supply a complete outfit, explain the missing category rather than inventing a garment. Treat saved preferences as soft guidance unless the user explicitly marks a restriction.",
